The source zip excludes node_modules, model weights and runtime binaries.
The following pinned dependencies are fetched into the app during setup:
- ffmpeg-static 5.3.0: GPL-3.0-or-later. Its FFmpeg binary is a separate
  executable downloaded from eugeneware/ffmpeg-static release b6.1.1.
  The corresponding README and licence accompany the installed binary.
  https://github.com/eugeneware/ffmpeg-static
- @huggingface/transformers 4.3.0: Apache-2.0.
  https://github.com/huggingface/transformers.js
Their transitive dependencies retain their original package licence files.
The bundled sample pictures (sample/take1.mp4 and take2.mp4) are already-generated
illustrative footage of a fictional presenter, with a "Synthetic demo" label added.
They are not a recording of a real person. Their generation record (Seedance 2.0,
fictional presenter from an existing clean reference; source clip sha256
9522e07bacf659877c71521d975ac0b88eee7c9fb9c318262aa93ea37a2db33f) is
evidence/aaa-phase/media/SOURCE.json in the development workspace. The sample
audio is Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0), described in sample/README.md.
The browser downloads the Xenova/whisper-tiny.en model on first speech
alignment. Model card: https://huggingface.co/Xenova/whisper-tiny.en
No FFmpeg code is copied into the app source. FFmpeg runs as a subprocess.


